From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:06:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] mtld3d: snmalloc-sys 0.7.6, vendored, takes GNU mode's
 ARM64EC for ARM64EC.

In GNU mode clang's ARM64EC defines __arm64ec__ and the x86-64 macros
but not MSVC's _M_ARM64EC, the one snmalloc tests: an ARM64EC half
whose C++ is built for arm64ec-w64-mingw32 took the x86 AAL and
memcpy.h's rep movsb inline assembly. aal/aal.h, aal/aal_arm.h and
global/memcpy.h test both. windows/Cargo.toml patches it in; every
other target compiles the same code as upstream's.

Assisted-by: Claude Code: claude-opus-5-5
